The `@app.route('/hello/<username>')` decorator is used to bind the `hello` function to the URL `/hello/<username>`. When a user visits this URL, Flask will call the `decorator` function with the `func` parameter set to the `hello` function, and then the wrapper function will be called with the correct parameters.

The `request.path.split('/')[2]` syntax is used to extract the username from the URL path. The `<username>` placeholder in the route decorator will match any string that follows the `/hello/` prefix, so we use this syntax to get the value of the `username` variable from the URL.

